SUMMARY:Agios Panteleimon and the greased-pole 'Stylos'\, Perama
LOCATION:Perama\, Lesvos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:In the old olive-oil port of Perama on the Gulf of Gera\, Agios Panteleimon (27 July) is celebrated with the 'Stylos': a greased log is fixed over the water on the pier with a flag at the end\, and young men try to walk out and grab it while the crowd cheers from the quay. Feast and music follow. Agios Panteleimon is also kept the same weekend at Skala Eresou (Portos)\, Apothika\, Megali Tsichranta and Plomari.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lesvos/#perama-agios-panteleimon-and-the-greased-pole-stylos-perama
